What does this print, and what are the final values of `state` and `result`?
```csharp
int state = 0;
int result = 99;
Func<int> f = () => ++state;
f += () =>
{
    Console.WriteLine(state);
    state += 10;
    throw new InvalidOperationException();
};
f += () => ++state;
try { result = f(); }
catch (InvalidOperationException)
{
    Console.WriteLine(state);
}
